    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2005208099397722422",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/2005208099397722422",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/2005208099397722422",
      "text": "[10:16AM] #Idunmota\n#Adeniji\n#TrafficUpdate\nThe stretch of Adeniji Adele road through Oba's palace down to Police post is looking good this morning.\n\nIlubinrin connecting Carter bridge inward Ijora Olopa as well as Oyingbo enroute Eko bridge is moving at a faster speed as there are no hindrances.\n\nIdumota underneath the bridge inward  Eyin Eyo connecting Balogun street is good as expected.\n\nThe fallen debris from the burnt building(Great Nigeria House) still spreads on the entire road on Martins Street, hence movement from Ereko street to connect Martins Street is totally restricted.\n\nTinubu square connecting Nnamdi Azikiwe street enroute Carter bridge on the return journey is good to go aside market activities along the  corridor.\n\nMeanwhile, our traffic personnel are  strategically positioned to ensure seamless traffic flow.\n#FollowLASTMA\n@Sola_Giwa\n@OlalekanOki\n@lagosMOT1 \n@TrafficChiefNG \n@trafficpalava \n@lagostraffic961",
